# 9. Attendance prediction business logic

You've implemented the reasoning for:

### Current attendance

```text
attended / total × 100
```

### Safe leaves

Simulation:

```text
attended stays the same
total increases by 1
```

until:

```text
attended / total < 0.75
```

### Recovery classes

Simulation:

```text
attended += 1
total += 1
```

until:

```text
attended / total >= 0.75
```

You've also understood why we make copies of the original database values rather than destroying them during the simulation.

And you caught the important attendance edge case:

> A timetable says a class was scheduled, but what if the class was actually cancelled?

So you designed attendance counting around actual attendance status rather than blindly assuming every timetable occurrence happened.

